title: Whispers in Ferraz
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: lead_rumours_due = 1 and lead_challenge_due = 0 and lead_forced_due = 0 and sanchez_leader = 1 and election_year = 0
on-arrival: lead_stage = 1

= Whispers in Ferraz

The stories start in the Madrid press: unnamed "historic leaders" and "senior figures in the federations" who doubt that Pedro Sánchez can win. Nobody puts a name to them yet. Everybody knows who they are.

- @r_ignore: Ignore it: rumours die if you do not feed them
- @r_address: Address it: meet the federations and the deputies one by one
- @r_bluff: Call their bluff: challenge the critics to say it to your face
- @r_primary: Call their bluff: call a leadership election yourself

@r_ignore
on-arrival: regional_leaders_dissent += 4; member_morale -= 2

The rumours do not die. They wait.

@r_address
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority += 5 + Q.member_morale / 12; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 3; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 3; Q.month_actions += 1; !}

A fortnight of meetings and phone calls. It buys time, and some of the barons are flattered to be asked.

@r_bluff
on-arrival: {!
Q.populism += 1; Q.lead_confronted = 1;
Q.bluff_won = (Q.federal_committee_balance + Q.member_morale / 4 + (Math.random() * 12 - 6) >= 55) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.bluff_won) { Q.sanchez_authority += 15; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 8; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 6; Q.sanchismo += 4; }
else { Q.sanchez_authority -= 12; Q.regional_leaders_dissent += 8; }
!}

[? if bluff_won = 1 : "If anyone wants my job, let them stand in a primary." Nobody does. For now, the critics retreat. ?][? if bluff_won = 0 : You dare them, and they take note. The critics are now openly counting votes in the Federal Committee. ?]

@r_primary
on-arrival: {! Q.populism += 1; Q.sanchismo += 3; window.SpainGame.leadershipElection(Q, 6); !}
go-to: primary_result

@primary_result
title: The leadership election

= The leadership election

[? if primary_won = 1 : The members vote, and they vote for you. With a fresh mandate from the rank and file, the critics have nothing left to say for a while. ?][? if primary_won = 0 : The members vote, and they choose [+ psoe_leader +]. Pedro Sánchez is no longer Secretary-General of the PSOE. ?]

@lead_challenge
title: A challenger emerges
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: lead_challenge_due = 1 and lead_forced_due = 0 and sanchez_leader = 1 and election_year = 0
on-arrival: lead_stage = 2

= A challenger emerges

The anonymous critics now have a name: [+ challenger +]. Seven regional federations are collecting signatures for an extraordinary leadership election, and the papers are already printing the arithmetic of the Federal Committee.

- @c_ignore: Ignore it and get on with the job
- @c_address: Address it: a speech to the parliamentary group, a tour of the federations
- @c_bluff: Call their bluff: dare them to table the motion in the Federal Committee
- @c_primary: Call their bluff: call the leadership election yourself, now

@c_ignore
on-arrival: sanchez_authority -= 5; regional_leaders_dissent += 6; federal_committee_balance -= 4

Silence looks like weakness. More signatures arrive.

@c_address
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchez_authority += 4 + Q.member_morale / 15; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 2; Q.federal_committee_balance += 2; Q.month_actions += 1; !}

You make your case. It steadies the group, but [+ challenger +] has not gone away.

@c_bluff
on-arrival: {!
Q.populism += 1; Q.lead_confronted = 1;
Q.bluff_won = (Q.federal_committee_balance + Q.member_morale / 4 + (Math.random() * 12 - 6) >= 60) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.bluff_won) { Q.sanchez_authority += 18; Q.regional_leaders_dissent -= 12; Q.sanchismo += 6; Q.lead_stage = 0; }
else { Q.sanchez_authority = Math.max(0, Q.sanchez_authority - 15); Q.federal_committee_balance -= 6; if (Math.random() < 0.4) { window.SpainGame.oust(Q, true); Q.bluff_expelled = 1; } }
!}

[? if bluff_won = 1 : The motion is never tabled. [+ challenger +] says there was never any challenge. ?][? if bluff_won = 0 : [? if bluff_expelled = 1 : The Federal Committee answers your dare by removing you, and the ethics committee opens proceedings for "disloyalty to the party's organs". You are expelled from the PSOE. ?][? if bluff_expelled = 0 : The critics table the motion. You survive the night, barely, and everyone knows the next vote is a matter of time. ?] ?]

@c_primary
on-arrival: {! Q.populism += 1; Q.sanchismo += 3; window.SpainGame.leadershipElection(Q, 5); !}
go-to: primary_result

@lead_forced
title: The forced primary
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: lead_forced_due = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1

= The forced primary

Your authority has collapsed. The Federal Committee convenes an extraordinary leadership election, and you cannot stop it. [+ challenger +] is the candidate of the federations. All that remains is to fight it.

- @f_fight: Fight for the members' votes
- @f_withdraw: Withdraw and leave with dignity

@f_fight
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.leadershipElection(Q, -3); if (!Q.primary_won && (Q.lead_confronted || Q.populism >= 6)) { Q.expelled = 1; } !}

[? if primary_won = 1 : Against every prediction, the members keep you. The apparatus is humiliated, and your authority is rebuilt from the ground up. ?][? if primary_won = 0 : [+ psoe_leader +] wins. [? if expelled = 1 : Within weeks your open war with the leadership ends in an expulsion file. You are no longer a member of the PSOE. ?] ?]

@f_withdraw
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.oust(Q, false); !}

You do not stand. [+ psoe_leader +] becomes Secretary-General unopposed.

@career_over
title: The end of the road
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: no_way_back = 1
go-to: game_over

@exile
title: After Ferraz
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: exile_pending = 1 and no_way_back = 0

= After Ferraz

[? if expelled = 1 : You have been expelled from the PSOE. ?][? if expelled = 0 : You are no longer Secretary-General. ?] What comes next depends on who still wants you.

[? if can_join_cs = 1 : Ciudadanos's leadership calls: a moderate who stood firm against independence, and a friend of the party, would be welcome. ?][? if can_join_up = 1 : Podemos calls: a radical, progressive, anti-establishment Sánchez could lead a broad front of the left. ?][? if can_found = 1 : Your followers are ready to start again under your own name: your pollsters think a Pedro Sánchez List could start at around [+ new_party_prospect +]%, though every vote it wins would come out of the PSOE or Podemos. ?]

[? if can_join_cs = 0 : Ciudadanos will not have you: it takes near-perfect relations (90+), a moderate economic line and a hard line against independence. ?] [? if can_join_up = 0 : Podemos will not have you: it takes near-perfect relations (90+), a progressive social line, a radical economic line and a populist style. ?] [? if can_found = 0 : There is no Sánchez movement to build a party on: that needs a dominant personal following. ?]

- @join_cs: Join Ciudadanos
- @join_up: Join Podemos
- @new_party: Found your own party
- @backbench: Stay in the PSOE as a backbench deputy and wait
- @retire: Retire from politics

@join_cs
view-if: can_join_cs = 1
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.joinParty(Q, 'cs'); Q.month_actions += 1; !}

You sign up with Ciudadanos at a packed press conference. The PSOE calls it treason; Rivera calls it the birth of a great centre. You will have to earn your place in a party that is not yours.

@join_up
view-if: can_join_up = 1
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.joinParty(Q, 'up'); Q.month_actions += 1; !}

You join Podemos's lists as an independent. The left calls it the end of the PSOE's monopoly; the PSOE calls it the end of Pedro Sánchez.

@new_party
view-if: can_found = 1
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.joinParty(Q, 'ps', 'Pedro Sánchez List'); Q.month_actions += 1; !}
go-to: founded

@founded
title: The founding

= The founding

[+ new_party_name +] is launched in a sports hall in Madrid. [? if populism >= 5 : Your anti-establishment message, "neither the apparatus nor the IBEX", fills it. ?][? if populism < 5 : The hall is respectable rather than full; you are known as a man of the apparatus you are now running against. ?] The first polls give it [+ player_poll +]%.

@backbench
view-if: expelled = 0
on-arrival: backbench = 1; backbench_since = time

You take a seat at the back of the PSOE group. The new leadership watches you as closely as the PP does. If they stumble, the members may remember you.

@retire
on-arrival: retired = 1

You leave politics, and write a book about it.

@comeback
title: The members remember
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: comeback_ready = 1 and backbench = 1 and election_year = 0

= The members remember

[? if comeback_forced = 1 : Your network has collected the signatures: the PSOE must hold an extraordinary leadership election. ?][? if comeback_forced = 0 : The PSOE under [+ psoe_leader +] is sinking in the polls. Members are signing a petition for a new primary, and many of them want you on the ballot. ?] Your campaign: network **[+ network_word +]**, barons won over [+ baron_allies +], war chest [+ war_chest +].

- @comeback_run: Run in the primary
- @comeback_wait: Not yet
- @comeback_leave: Leave the PSOE for good

@comeback_run
on-arrival: {! var b = Q.backbench_since; Q.comeback_forced = 0; window.SpainGame.leadershipElection(Q, 4 + window.SpainGame.comebackBonus(Q)); if (!Q.primary_won) { Q.backbench = 1; Q.backbench_since = b; Q.comeback_next = Q.time + 24; Q.network = Math.round((Q.network || 0) * 0.6); } !}

[? if primary_won = 1 : Pedro Sánchez is Secretary-General of the PSOE again. The barons who threw you out will have to work with you. ?][? if primary_won = 0 : [+ psoe_leader +] holds on. The members were tempted, not convinced. ?]

@comeback_wait
on-arrival: comeback_next = time + 6

You let them sign. The longer they wait, the louder they will ask.

@comeback_leave
on-arrival: backbench = 0; backbench_since = 0

You hand in your membership card. The question is where to go next.

@player_line
title: How will your party vote?
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: exiled = 1 and acting = 1 and election_year = 0 and player_line_set = 0 and formation_weeks >= 1

= How will [+ my_party +] vote?

Congress is hung. [? if player_is_right_cand = 1 : As the largest party of the right, you are the right's candidate; ?][? if player_is_right_cand = 0 : [+ right_leader +] is the right's candidate; ?] [+ psoe_leader +] leads the PSOE. With [+ player_seats +] deputies, [+ my_party +] has to choose. [? if player_is_ps = 1 : [? if player_seats > congress_psoe_seats : Your party is bigger than the PSOE: the left's candidate would be you. ?] ?]

- @line_right_coalition: [? if player_is_right_cand = 1 : Stand as the right's candidate, in coalition with the PP ?][? if player_is_right_cand = 0 : Enter a coalition government with [+ right_leader +] ?]
- @line_right_support: [? if player_is_right_cand = 1 : Stand as the right's candidate, alone ?][? if player_is_right_cand = 0 : Support [+ right_leader +] from outside ?]
- @line_left_coalition: Enter a coalition government with the PSOE
- @line_left_support: Support the PSOE's candidate from outside, abstain on the right's
- @line_abstain: Abstain on every candidate
- @line_against: Vote against every candidate and force new elections

@line_right_coalition
choose-if: player_is_cs = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Only Ciudadanos would join the right in government.
on-arrival: {! Q.player_line_right = 'coalition'; Q.player_line_left = 'no'; Q.player_line_set = 1; Q.rel_pp += 5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, -0.5); } !}

Ministries in exchange for your votes. Your old comrades will never forgive the photograph.

@line_right_support
on-arrival: {! Q.player_line_right = 'support'; Q.player_line_left = 'no'; Q.player_line_set = 1; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.5, 0); } !}

Your deputies will vote for [+ right_leader +], in exchange for a programme.

@line_left_coalition
choose-if: player_is_cs = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Ciudadanos will not sit in a cabinet with the PSOE.
on-arrival: {! Q.player_line_left = 'coalition'; Q.player_line_right = 'no'; Q.player_line_set = 1; Q.rel_psoe = (Q.rel_psoe || 20) + 5; !}

You offer the PSOE a coalition. The irony is not lost on anyone.

@line_left_support
on-arrival: {! Q.player_line_left = 'support'; Q.player_line_right = 'abstain'; Q.player_line_set = 1; !}

Support for the PSOE's candidate, without joining the government.

@line_abstain
on-arrival: {! Q.player_line_left = 'abstain'; Q.player_line_right = 'abstain'; Q.player_line_set = 1; !}

Your deputies will abstain and let the others decide.

@line_against
on-arrival: {! Q.player_line_left = 'no'; Q.player_line_right = 'no'; Q.player_line_set = 1; Q.populism += 1; !}

No to everyone. If nobody else can count to 176, Spain will vote again.

@auto_government
title: A government is formed
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: auto_formed = 1
on-arrival: auto_formed = 0

= A government is formed

Congress invests [+ pm +]. Spain has a [+ government_type +]. [? if player_in_government = 1 : [+ my_party +] is in government. ?][? if sanchez_pm = 1 : Pedro Sánchez is Prime Minister. ?]

@pp_leader_falls
title: The PP changes leader
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: pp_leader_falls_due = 1 and election_year = 0
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.choosePPLeader(Q); !}

= The PP changes leader

[+ pp_old_leader +] has lost [? if pm_is_pp = 0 : the government ?][? if pm_is_pp = 1 : the party's confidence ?], and the PP will not forgive it. After weeks of pressure from the regional barons, [+ pp_old_leader +] resigns. The party congress chooses [+ pp_leader +].

[? if pp_style_hard = 1 : The new leader promises to recover the voters who left for Vox: a harder line on Catalonia, on taxes and on immigration. Vox's leaders smile; the PNV stops returning calls. ?][? if pp_style_moderate = 1 : The new leader promises a calmer, more centrist PP, open to State pacts. Ciudadanos's voters start coming home; Vox calls it the "cowardly right". ?]

- @pp_pact: Offer the new leader a State pact on pensions and Catalonia
- @pp_same: "Same PP, new face": tie them to the corruption of the past
- @pp_wait: Watch and wait

@pp_pact
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pp += 8; Q.progressives_dissent += 5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, -0.3, 0); } !}

The offer is received politely and declined politely. Moderate voters noticed it was made.

@pp_same
on-arrival: {! Q.rel_pp -= 6; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.target(Q, 'psoe', 'young', 1); } !}

The corruption files are reopened on every talk show.

@pp_wait
on-arrival: institutionalists_dissent -= 1

You let the new leader make the first mistakes.

@barons_coup
title: The barons move
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: coup_due = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1 and rebellion_used = 0
on-arrival: rebellion_used = 1

= The rebellion

It happens on a Wednesday afternoon. The critics' aim is to stop your primaries and your congress before they can happen. Seventeen members of the Federal Executive resign at once to force the Executive to dissolve. Verónica Pérez, President of the Federal Committee and Susana Díaz's closest ally in Seville, tells the cameras outside Ferraz that she is now "the only authority in the party". Behind her stand the regional leaders: Susana Díaz, Emiliano García-Page, Javier Lambán, Guillermo Fernández Vara. They say the PSOE cannot go on losing elections under Pedro Sánchez. [? if acting = 1 : They also want the PSOE to stop blocking a government. ?]

[? if loyalist_posts >= 4 : Your own people hold enough posts in Ferraz and in the federations to put up a fight. ?][? if loyalist_posts < 4 : You have few loyalists in the party's structures; the apparatus belongs to them. ?]

- @coup_refuse: Refuse to recognise the resignations: the Executive continues "in functions"
- @coup_fight: Go straight to the Federal Committee and fight it out
- @coup_members: Appeal over their heads: call a primary of the members now
- @coup_resign: Resign rather than split the party

@coup_refuse
on-arrival: {! Q.two_authorities = 1; Q.sanchismo += 3; Q.plot += 3; !}

César Luena, your Secretary of Organisation, tells the press that you remain the legitimate Secretary-General: resignations do not remove a leader elected by the members. The country now watches a party with two leaderships.

@coup_fight
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.baronsCoup(Q, 'fight'); Q.lead_confronted = 1; !}

[? if coup_survived = 1 : After eleven hours of shouting behind closed doors, the vote goes your way. The plotters retreat to their federations, humiliated, and the party knows who is in charge. ?][? if coup_survived = 0 : After eleven hours behind closed doors, you lose the vote. You resign as Secretary-General. A caretaker committee under [+ psoe_leader +] takes over Ferraz. [? if acting = 1 : [? if gestora_abstains = 1 : Its first decision will be to let the PP govern. ?] ?] ?]

@coup_members
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.baronsCoup(Q, 'members'); Q.populism += 1; !}

[? if coup_survived = 1 : The members answer you, not the barons. With a fresh mandate, the plot collapses. ?][? if coup_survived = 0 : The members do not save you. A caretaker committee under [+ psoe_leader +] takes over. ?]

@coup_resign
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.baronsCoup(Q, 'resign'); !}

You resign to avoid a split. A caretaker committee under [+ psoe_leader +] takes over Ferraz. [? if acting = 1 : [? if gestora_abstains = 1 : Its first decision will be to let the PP govern. ?] ?]

@gestora_abstains
title: The caretaker committee abstains
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: psoe_interim = 1 and gestora_abstains = 1 and acting = 1 and election_year = 0 and gestora_seen_round < formation_round
on-arrival: {! Q.gestora_seen_round = Q.formation_round || 1; !}

= The caretaker committee abstains

The caretaker committee led by [+ psoe_leader +] takes the question to the Federal Committee: should the PSOE abstain and let [+ right_leader +] govern? [+ psoe_leader +] insists that abstaining is not the same as supporting the PP. The Committee votes for abstention by a clear margin[? if year = 2016 : , 139 to 96 ?]. The Catalan socialists announce they will not follow the instruction. Your supporters fill the street outside Ferraz chanting "No es no" ("No means no"), and you call on the members to rebuild a party that does not prop up the right.

@vara_breaks_ranks
title: A baron breaks ranks
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: sanchez_leader = 1 and acting = 1 and plot >= 40 and coup_due = 0 and vara_seen = 0 and rebellion_used = 0 and elections_held >= 1
on-arrival: {! Q.vara_seen = 1; !}

= A baron breaks ranks

Guillermo Fernández Vara, President of Extremadura, says in public what the barons have been saying in private: another general election would be bad for Spain and worse for the PSOE, and the party cannot keep up an unconditional no. He asks for a Federal Committee to discuss it.

- @vara_debate: Agree to a Federal Committee debate on the strategy
- @vara_dismiss: Dismiss him: the members gave you the mandate
- @vara_alternative: Ask the Committee for authority to explore an alternative government

@vara_debate
on-arrival: {! Q.plot -= 5; Q.federal_committee_balance += 3; Q.sanchez_authority -= 2; !}

The debate is scheduled. It buys time, and the barons note that you blinked.

@vara_dismiss
on-arrival: {! Q.plot += 8; Q.sanchismo += 2; Q.member_morale += 2; !}

Your supporters cheer. The barons start coordinating.

@vara_alternative
on-arrival: {! Q.plot += 5; Q.alt_gov_bid = 1; Q.rel_up += 3; Q.up_talks += 0.5; if (window.SpainGame) { window.SpainGame.position(Q, 0.3, 0); } !}

You want a mandate to talk to Podemos and, perhaps, Ciudadanos. The critics say any government that depends on Podemos and the Catalan independence parties is no government at all.

@page_attacks
title: García-Page attacks
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: sanchez_leader = 1 and acting = 1 and plot >= 50 and coup_due = 0 and page_seen = 0 and vara_seen = 1 and rebellion_used = 0
on-arrival: {! Q.page_seen = 1; !}

= García-Page attacks

Emiliano García-Page, President of Castilla-La Mancha, accuses you of treating dissenting colleagues unfairly and demands a Federal Congress. The two camps are organising around rival strategies: yours, of rejecting the right and exploring an alternative; theirs, of letting the right govern to end the deadlock.

- @page_primaries: Call primaries and a Federal Congress now: let the members decide
- @page_abide: Promise to abide by whatever the Federal Committee decides
- @page_ignore: Ignore him

@page_primaries
on-arrival: {! Q.primaries_called = 1; Q.plot += 12; Q.sanchismo += 4; Q.populism += 1; !}

You announce primaries within a month, followed by a Federal Congress. It is a direct appeal to the members before the deadlock can be resolved without you, and the barons see it as a declaration of war. They start discussing mass resignations from the Executive to stop it.

@page_abide
on-arrival: {! Q.plot -= 10; Q.sanchez_authority -= 8; Q.federal_committee_balance += 4; Q.psoe_stance_pp = 'abstain'; !}

You defuse the rebellion by handing the decision to the Federal Committee, which everyone knows will choose abstention. Your members ask what you are for.

@page_ignore
on-arrival: plot += 4

The critics take your silence as weakness.

@felipe_speaks
title: Felipe González speaks
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: sanchez_leader = 1 and acting = 1 and plot >= 50 and felipe_seen = 0 and rebellion_used = 0 and year <= 2019
on-arrival: {! Q.felipe_seen = 1; !}

= Felipe González speaks

On morning radio, Felipe González, the PSOE's most famous former prime minister, says he feels "cheated": you told him privately, he says, that you would abstain to let Rajoy govern. The old guard rallies behind him.

- @felipe_deny: Deny it flatly, on air, the same morning
- @felipe_silence: Say nothing: you will not fight Felipe in public

@felipe_deny
on-arrival: {! Q.plot += 6; Q.sanchismo += 3; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 6; !}

Your members love it. The old guard will not forgive it.

@felipe_silence
on-arrival: {! Q.plot += 3; Q.sanchez_authority -= 3; !}

His version becomes the story.

@two_authorities_event
title: Two authorities
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: two_authorities = 1 and sanchez_leader = 1
on-arrival: {! Q.two_authorities = 0; !}

= Two authorities

The party now has two leaderships. Your remaining Executive says it continues in functions; Verónica Pérez says it has ceased to exist and that she is "the only authority" until a caretaker committee takes over. Susana Díaz offers herself as the person who can bring the party together, and rejects a congress "designed around one man". Both sides call the Federal Committee for Saturday morning at Ferraz.

- @auth_condition: Announce that you will resign if the Committee votes for abstention
- @auth_rules: Fight on procedure: dispute Verónica Pérez's authority over the Committee
- @auth_compromise: Offer a compromise: a congress later, in exchange for no abstention now

@auth_condition
on-arrival: {! Q.fc_bonus = 6; Q.sanchismo += 3; !}
go-to: federal_committee_day

@auth_rules
on-arrival: {! Q.fc_bonus = 3; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 5; !}
go-to: federal_committee_day

@auth_compromise
on-arrival: {! Q.fc_bonus = 8; Q.sanchez_authority -= 5; Q.plot -= 5; !}
go-to: federal_committee_day

@federal_committee_day
title: The Federal Committee
new-page: true

= Saturday: the Federal Committee

At nine in the morning you slip into Ferraz past the waiting press. More than 250 members of the Federal Committee crowd the hall; the meeting starts an hour and a half late, after arguments over who chairs it. Before eleven-thirty the critics refuse to recognise your seventeen remaining Executive members' right to vote. At a quarter to one Verónica Pérez's Mesa takes its seats. A hundred and fifty members ask to speak.

By three in the afternoon you propose yet another Committee meeting. Javier Lambán answers that you are no longer Secretary-General. By six your supporters set up a ballot box to vote on an extraordinary congress; the critics call it illegal.

- @fc_ballot: Insist on the ballot box: a secret vote
- @fc_hands: Accept a public vote by show of hands

@fc_ballot
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.federalCommitteeVote(Q, (Q.fc_bonus || 0) - 2); !}
go-to: fc_result

@fc_hands
on-arrival: {! window.SpainGame.federalCommitteeVote(Q, (Q.fc_bonus || 0) + 1); !}
go-to: fc_result

@fc_result
title: The vote

= The vote

[? if coup_survived = 1 : Shortly after eight in the evening the vote is counted: [+ fc_for +] for the extraordinary congress, [+ fc_against +] against. You have won. The critics walk out into the night; Verónica Pérez's Mesa dissolves itself. The barons will need years to try again. ?][? if coup_survived = 0 : Shortly after eight in the evening the vote is counted: [+ fc_against +] against the extraordinary congress, [+ fc_for +] for. Ten minutes later you announce your resignation as Secretary-General. At nine you face the press. The Committee appoints a caretaker committee under [+ psoe_leader +] to run the party until a new congress. ?]

@seat_choice
title: The second vote
new-page: true
tags: sp_event
view-if: gestora_invested = 1 and seat_choice_done = 0 and sanchez_leader = 0 and exiled = 0
on-arrival: seat_choice_done = 1

= The second vote

The caretaker committee has won the Federal Committee vote to abstain. In the first investiture vote the socialists vote no; in the second, they are to abstain and let [+ pm +] govern. [+ psoe_rebels +] socialist deputies, including all the Catalan socialists, say they will vote no anyway. On the morning of the vote, you have to decide what you will do with your own seat.

- @seat_resign: Give up your seat rather than abstain
- @seat_rebel: Keep your seat and vote no with the rebels
- @seat_abstain: Abstain with the group

@seat_resign
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchismo += 10; Q.member_morale += 4; Q.populism += 1; Q.seat_resigned = 1; !}

You resign as a deputy, saying you cannot vote for what you promised you would never allow. You walk out of Congress with nothing but the members' sympathy, which is everything you need for a comeback.

@seat_rebel
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchismo += 6; Q.institutionalists_dissent += 6; Q.expelled_risk = 1; !}

You vote no with the rebels. The caretaker committee opens disciplinary proceedings against all of you.

@seat_abstain
on-arrival: {! Q.sanchismo -= 12; Q.member_morale -= 6; Q.institutionalists_dissent -= 4; !}

You abstain with the group. The members who were chanting your name outside Ferraz feel betrayed.
